{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe rain here is relentless, turning the streets into rivers, but I could not rest. After lunch, I hired a carriage to Nussdorf despite the weather. The air was thick and heavy, yet I felt a strange lightness. On the road, I saw a large pear tree, its fruit long since harvested, yet it was in full blossom again. It seemed absurd, a defiance of the natural order, but there was a certain stubborn vitality in it. I enclosed two of the blossoms in this letter for you. They are not beautiful, but they are a sign that life persists even when it seems out of place or out of season.\n\nI think of you and the boys often. The journey is wearying, but the mind is active. I hope the news finds you well. I shall write again soon.\n\nYours,\nGeorg Wilhelm"}}],"created":1795080422,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":183,"prompt_tokens":938,"total_tokens":1121,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-WeS2VAZsuT9WV6z5ShErvVIIcxRkENDs","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":938,"prompt_ms":994.498,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.060232409381663,"prompt_per_second":943.1894282341441,"predicted_n":183,"predicted_ms":4384.705,"predicted_per_token_ms":24.091785714285713,"predicted_per_second":41.50792356612361}}